### 2026-08-29T17:45:46.690Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

Confirmed exactly. Here's the report:

**Why pasting into Gravity failed**: `GravityMode.pasteClipboard` silently does nothing (no error, no message, no visual feedback) whenever *every* cell being pasted lands on an already-occupied position — `if (!placed.length) return;` in `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]`. I reproduced this precisely: copying Gravity's own current board and immediately pasting it back (copy → paste, same mode, no other action in between) leaves the board completely unchanged, with the clipboard correctly populated (3 cells copied) but zero cells actually placed.

The replay's own event sequence matches this closely — a `#copy-btn` click, followed by mode-switching around the drawer, then repeated `#paste-btn` clicks (2 the first time, 5 the second, out of evident frustration that nothing was visibly happening). Whatever was copied, its cells' positions in Gravity's coordinate space were already occupied (either because it was copied from Gravity's own board and pasted right back onto itself, or because a paste from another mode landed on cells the current pile already fills) — either way, the paste is entirely rejected with no indication to the player of *why*.

This isn't a broken feature — copy/paste into Gravity works correctly when there's actually empty space to paste into (there's a passing test covering exactly that). The real gap is **the total silence on a fully-blocked paste** — a player has no way to tell "nothing happened because you pasted a bug" apart from "the button doesn't work." Not committing anything since this was a diagnosis, not a fix — let me know if you want the silent-no-op turned into a real UI signal (e.g., a brief shake/flash on the paste button, matching how `flashClipboardButton` already confirms a *successful* paste).


